WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.571
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:09.629
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:16.679
Unit fourteen: Advanced Passive Structures. Today you will report opinions and facts in an objective, formal tone.

4
00:00:16.979 --> 00:00:19.678
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:23.750
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:25.827
Is said to be.

7
00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:29.722
Is said to be means a passive reporting structure.

8
00:00:30.317 --> 00:00:31.724
He is said to be rich.

9
00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:35.341
Your turn. Say: Is said to be.

10
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.398
Is said to be.

11
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:41.395
Is believed to be.

12
00:00:42.383 --> 00:00:45.405
Is believed to be means a passive reporting structure.

13
00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:47.633
It is believed to be safe.

14
00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:51.658
Your turn. Say: Is believed to be.

15
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.838
Is believed to be.

16
00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:57.944
Reported passive.

17
00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.447
Reported passive means a passive used to report opinions.

18
00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.015
A reported passive sentence.

19
00:01:05.617 --> 00:01:08.838
Your turn. Say: Reported passive.

20
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.165
Reported passive.

21
00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:15.440
Passive with modals.

22
00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:20.272
Passive with modals means modal + be + past participle.

23
00:01:20.883 --> 00:01:22.175
It must be done.

24
00:01:22.783 --> 00:01:25.877
Your turn. Say: Passive with modals.

25
00:01:28.733 --> 00:01:30.210
Passive with modals.

26
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:32.218
It is thought that.

27
00:01:33.217 --> 00:01:36.284
It is thought that means an impersonal opinion structure.

28
00:01:36.883 --> 00:01:39.115
It is thought that prices will rise.

29
00:01:39.717 --> 00:01:42.508
Your turn. Say: It is thought that.

30
00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:46.844
It is thought that.

31
00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:48.944
Formal passive.

32
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:53.076
Formal passive means a style used in reports.

33
00:01:53.683 --> 00:01:55.207
A formal passive.

34
00:01:55.817 --> 00:01:58.933
Your turn. Say: Formal passive.

35
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.033
Formal passive.

36
00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:04.889
Impersonal.

37
00:02:05.883 --> 00:02:08.533
Impersonal means not focused on a person.

38
00:02:09.117 --> 00:02:10.803
An impersonal style.

39
00:02:11.417 --> 00:02:13.872
Your turn. Say: Impersonal.

40
00:02:16.733 --> 00:02:17.920
Impersonal.

41
00:02:18.683 --> 00:02:20.091
Objective tone.

42
00:02:21.083 --> 00:02:24.337
Objective tone means neutral, without personal opinion.

43
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.427
An objective tone.

44
00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:29.750
Your turn. Say: Objective tone.

45
00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:33.891
Objective tone.

46
00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.560
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:43.483
Visal, how can you report an opinion without saying who thinks it?

48
00:02:44.583 --> 00:02:55.920
We say It is thought that prices will rise, or Prices are thought to rise. These reported passives sound objective and formal, so they are common in news and academic writing.

49
00:02:57.017 --> 00:02:58.354
How are they formed?

50
00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:13.213
Subject + is said, believed, thought, known, reported + to-infinitive: The company is said to be profitable. For past events use the perfect infinitive: He is believed to have left.

51
00:03:14.317 --> 00:03:15.306
Why use them?

52
00:03:16.417 --> 00:03:28.058
They hide the speaker and present information as general. They also allow us to put new information at the end. Use them carefully, since vague claims may hide who actually made the statement.

53
00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.828
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:31.683 --> 00:03:36.678
Grammar focus: Reported passive: It is said that… and He is said to….

55
00:03:36.978 --> 00:03:38.246
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:41.228
The company is said to be very profitable.

57
00:03:42.117 --> 00:03:44.302
It is thought that prices will rise.

58
00:03:45.217 --> 00:03:47.181
He is believed to have left the country.

59
00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:55.987
Subject + is said / believed / thought + to-infinitive, or It is said that + clause. Use the perfect infinitive for past events.

60
00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.203
Be careful! Don't say: It says that he is rich person.

61
00:04:02.167 --> 00:04:04.549
Say: He is said to be rich.

62
00:04:04.849 --> 00:04:06.245
Use is said to be.

63
00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:09.790
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.112
Objective Reporting.

65
00:04:12.412 --> 00:04:14.818
The company is said to be very profitable.

66
00:04:15.833 --> 00:04:19.214
It is believed that the bridge is more than a hundred years old.

67
00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.815
He is reported to have left the country last night.

68
00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.496
It is thought that prices will rise next year.

69
00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.138
This formal passive keeps an objective tone.

70
00:04:31.233 --> 00:04:35.131
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:35.983 --> 00:04:38.111
The painting is blank to be very old.

72
00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:41.658
A, said. B, say. C, saying.

73
00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.758
The answer is A: said.

74
00:04:47.917 --> 00:04:49.812
It blank that the plan will fail.

75
00:04:50.112 --> 00:04:53.684
A, is thought. B, thinks. C, is thinking.

76
00:04:57.233 --> 00:04:59.082
The answer is A: is thought.

77
00:05:00.217 --> 00:05:03.206
He is believed blank left yesterday. (past)

78
00:05:03.506 --> 00:05:06.811
A, to have. B, to. C, having.

79
00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:12.680
The answer is A: to have.

80
00:05:13.817 --> 00:05:15.572
Which sentence is impersonal?

81
00:05:15.872 --> 00:05:22.138
A, I think prices will rise.. B, It is thought that prices will rise.. C, You think prices rise..

82
00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.244
The answer is B: It is thought that prices will rise..

83
00:05:30.383 --> 00:05:33.242
According to the reading, how old is the bridge?

84
00:05:33.542 --> 00:05:38.380
A, over a hundred years. B, ten years. C, fifty years.

85
00:05:41.933 --> 00:05:44.502
The answer is A: over a hundred years.

86
00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.875
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:49.717 --> 00:05:54.038
Rewrite an opinion as an objective passive statement, like 'It is thought that...'.

88
00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.257
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:04.557 --> 00:06:16.001
Original: People think the new policy will help farmers. Passive: It is thought that the new policy will help farmers. The statement is now impersonal and sounds more objective.

90
00:06:16.301 --> 00:06:18.103
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:19.017 --> 00:06:25.547
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reported passive: it is said that… and he is said to….

92
00:06:25.847 --> 00:06:30.391
Today's value is critical reasoning. Test every argument before you accept it.

93
00:06:30.691 --> 00:06:33.309
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:33.609 --> 00:06:36.377
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

